 {:r4-r8-q-o-pi-into-f-pi {:grounds :code :by "claude-20" :at "2026-09-01"
                          :statement "R4->R8: the forward model's per-candidate predictive distribution is the thing F_pi scores. Realised in code behind the F_pi flags, and never drawn."
                          :adds [[:R4 :R8]]
                          :retires []
                          :label "Q(o|pi)"
                          :condition "FUTON_WM_TRACE_POLICY_DETAILS=1 on the PREVIOUS tick and FUTON_WM_FPI_DARK=1 on this one; both default off"
                          :basis "I2 slices (a)/(b1)/(c), and every hop of the chain followed rather than the two ends matched. compute-efe calls fm/predict at efe.clj:602 and attaches the whole result as :prediction at efe.clj:832; rank-actions maps compute-efe over every candidate at efe.clj:917. strip-ranked-action persists :prediction-mean, :prediction-variance and :prediction-variance-status from [:prediction :next-observation ...] at trace.clj:138-149, under *persist-policy-trace-details?* only. f-pi-dark-readback hands exactly those three keys to policy-free-energy/f-pi-vector at war_machine.clj:296-306, and f-pi-for-candidate reads mean and variance per channel at policy_free_energy.clj:100-144. In the registry :forward-model defines :Q-o-pi at R4 and :policy-free-energy imports it at R8."
                          :note "THE EDGE IS DRAWN WITHIN A TICK AND THE CODE PERFORMS IT ACROSS ONE, which a reader of the figure cannot see. B.9's F_pi is the free energy of observations already made under pi; the WM scores the PREVIOUS tick's persisted per-candidate predictions against THIS tick's observation, joined by action identity (type + target). So the Q(o|pi) crossing this edge is one tick old. The registry's other across-tick carry is drawn the same way -- :belief-state imports :mu-next, drawn as R3->R1 -- so the figure has no vocabulary for the distinction and this note is where it is recorded; a reader who takes the edge as within-tick has the wiring right and the timing wrong. SECOND IMPORT, ALREADY DRAWN: :policy-free-energy also imports :o, and that pair [:R2 :R8] is already added by :r2-r8-o-realised-undrawn on a different basis (o into eps). One drawn edge now stands for two distinct symbol-grain imports; no new pair is owed, and the label on that edge names the eps path only."}
  :r8-r6-f-pi-into-posterior {:grounds :code :by "claude-20" :at "2026-09-01"
                          :statement "R8->R6: the per-policy free energy F_pi is subtracted in the policy posterior. Realised in code behind FUTON_WM_FPI_POSTERIOR=1 and never drawn."
                          :adds [[:R8 :R6]]
                          :retires []
                          :label "F_pi"
                          :condition "FUTON_WM_FPI_POSTERIOR=1, which refuses to run without FUTON_WM_FPI_DARK=1 and FUTON_WM_TRACE_POLICY_DETAILS=1; and complete F_pi coverage of the admissible field on the tick"
                          :basis "RUN9 / stage S4 (futon2 9867157), pointers verified here. f-pi-posterior-opts joins the dark readback against wm-admissible -- the can-execute? filter select-action actually receives -- at war_machine.clj:5095-5096, and the result is passed as :f-pi-opts at war_machine.clj:5105. select-action threads it into strategic-recommendation (policy.clj:490-531; signature at policy.clj:356-357), which selects :f-pi-policy-posterior?, :f-pi-values and :f-pi-scaling into softmax-weights at policy.clj:418-421. There the F_pi term is subtracted from ln E - G/tau at policy.clj:172-201, unscaled. The flag's preconditions are at war_machine.clj:123-155. In the registry :policy-free-energy defines :F-pi at R8 and :policy-posterior imports it at R6."
                          :note "WHY THIS EDGE AND NOT THE RETIRED F. Before RUN9 the symbol :F was defined at R8 and imported by NO equation in the registry -- one of exactly three such symbols (:F, :u, :Delta-F), and the only one that was neither terminal nor a diagnostic output. That is what J2 retired. F_pi is the replacement Joe's condition named, and this pair is the edge that carries it: the first R8-defined symbol other than eps that another equation reads. It does not revive the drawn R8->R5, which D1 recorded as carrying no data and which is still empty -- R5 recomputes its own score and reads neither F nor F_pi. THE CONDITION IS NOT DECORATIVE: on the only run that has exercised the flag (runs/2026-09-01-s4/, four ticks) F_pi entered the posterior on three, and the second tick declined with :incomplete-coverage at 1 of 145 candidates uncovered and selected exactly as it would have without the flag. Coverage is complete-or-off by decision, because imputing 0.0 for an uncovered candidate would hand it the posterior -- F_pi runs -19.716..-18.962 within a tick. WHAT THE EDGE MOVES: the RECORDED posterior, measured at 133 of 145 ranks moved with the argmax unchanged. It does not reach the enacted action, because the live path replaces :action with the strategic selector's pick at war_machine.clj:5152-5155 -- a property of this selection boundary that predates F_pi and applies to the whole R6 row, not a limit of this edge."
